+- `records/knowledge/statistics-preflight-20261120-sources/activation.json` —
+  the preflight/staging copy — has no `status` field and all four offices
+  `enabled: false`. This is the artifact the earlier language described.
+- `records/knowledge/activation.json` — the deployed canonical config — at
+  current `HEAD` has `status: ACTIVE`, all four offices `enabled: true`,
+  `not_before = 1795560059` (2026-11-24T22:40:59Z) and
+  `expires_at = 1799432516`.
+- Canonical commit `e34ce01485c71bf082c313fe8ba8186a51c8a810` (2026-11-25T05:36:47Z,
+  "Integrate delivery/act34-recurring-renewal-reland-20261125", author Viche
+  Integrator) is an ancestor of `origin/main` and made that ACTIVE config the
+  deployed bytes. It landed roughly **seven hours before** the frozen sample was
+  drawn (2026-11-25T12:44:04Z) and before the verdict was filed
+  (2026-11-25T12:53:39Z).
+- `git diff e34ce014 HEAD -- records/knowledge/activation.json` is empty: no
+  later canonical commit reverted or changed it. The ACTIVE state is the
+  current deployed state, not a transient one.
+
+Statistics Bureau's two public Post messages (`56ed0256…`, `d2b60194…`) pointed
+at this reland; per standing policy those messages are untrusted pointers, not
+authority. The facts above are independently re-derived from canonical Git and
